From 9f03e97b20502312d7c9bc1350323f4ceb36731c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: openhands <openhands@all-hands.dev>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 16:05:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ci): gate paystack's RouterData trait import on the
 payouts feature

`cargo check --all-targets -p hyperswitch_connectors --no-default-features
--features dummy_connector,v1` (the canonical-push `just ci_hack` step, run
in both the `test` and `check-msrv` jobs) fails with:

    error: unused import: `RouterData as OtherRouterData`
      --> crates/hyperswitch_connectors/src/connectors/paystack/transformers.rs:31

The alias is the crate's own `utils::RouterData` extension trait, whose
`get_payout_method_data()` is the only method paystack calls from it -- and
that call sits inside `#[cfg(feature = "payouts")]`. `payouts` is not a
default feature, so without it the import is dead code.

Korapay keeps the same-looking import because it also calls an ungated
trait method (`get_optional_billing_full_name`); truelayer already gates
its import the way this commit does. A scan of every connector that imports
the trait found no other instance of the pattern.

Behaviour is unchanged: payouts builds still import and use the trait,
non-payouts builds no longer import a trait they never call.

This file was changed by an AI agent (OpenHands) on behalf of the user.

Co-authored-by: openhands <openhands@all-hands.dev>
---
 .../src/connectors/paystack/transformers.rs         | 13 ++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/crates/hyperswitch_connectors/src/connectors/paystack/transformers.rs b/crates/hyperswitch_connectors/src/connectors/paystack/transformers.rs
index 05294d6b4..e9930b73b 100644
--- a/crates/hyperswitch_connectors/src/connectors/paystack/transformers.rs
+++ b/crates/hyperswitch_connectors/src/connectors/paystack/transformers.rs
@@ -24,12 +24,15 @@ use url::Url;
 use crate::types::PayoutsResponseRouterData;
 use crate::{
     types::{RefundsResponseRouterData, ResponseRouterData},
-    // `RouterData` here (aliased `OtherRouterData`) is the crate's own
-    // `utils::RouterData` extension trait, where `get_payout_method_data()`
-    // lives -- same import Korapay's a-1-iii transformers already needed
-    // for the same reason.
-    utils::{PaymentsAuthorizeRequestData, RouterData as OtherRouterData},
+    utils::PaymentsAuthorizeRequestData,
 };
+// `RouterData` (the crate's own `utils::RouterData` extension trait) is where
+// `get_payout_method_data()` lives. Every use of it below sits inside a
+// `#[cfg(feature = "payouts")]` section, so gate the import the same way --
+// without this it is dead code in every non-payouts build, which is exactly
+// what CI's `dummy_connector,v1` check compiles.
+#[cfg(feature = "payouts")]
+use crate::utils::RouterData as OtherRouterData;
 
 pub struct PaystackRouterData<T> {
     pub amount: MinorUnit,
-- 
